1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
This is Recall Response Workbench. The guided rehearsal evaluates the same deterministic fixture used by the WebMCP tools.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
8,420 candidate orders collapse to exactly 37 affected orders.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The safety-critical number is 213. Those orders carry L24-019, a lookalike that is not the affected lot L24-091.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The workbench explicitly excludes every one of those lookalikes.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Rehearsal is only a fast preview. It uses the same domain service and visible state, but it is not a WebMCP substitute.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The evidence trail starts with recall RC-2026-014 and exact supplier lot L24-091.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,000
A strict equality filter records 37 matches, 213 exclusions, and representative matched orders.

8
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The 37 affected orders resolve to 10 warehouse, 9 in-transit, 9 delivered, and 9 already-returned orders.

9
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Each receives one classification: quarantine, intercept, contact, or completed return.

10
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The app stages 10 quarantines, 9 carrier intercept requests, and 18 customer outreach drafts.

11
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Nothing is committed or sent. Durable actions remain zero.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Now I use real Codex Site Tools. The top-level page registers imperative WebMCP tools.

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:59,000
I ask Codex to trace the exact lot, classify the affected orders, and stage a review without committing or sending.

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Codex invokes one registered atomic tool set. Domain preconditions enforce order, and the visible page updates before results return.

15
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:18,000
An attempt to use L24-019 is rejected and corrected to affected lot L24-091.

16
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Codex stops at staged review. There is no WebMCP confirm, commit, or send tool.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,000
I inspect the evidence and activate the visible normal page control.

18
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Codex reads the current rehearsal receipt and non-cryptographic demo checksum. Reset clears both.
